<title>USA: Sheboygan, Wis., won by First of America. [Corrected 17:47 gmt]</title>
<headline>Sheboygan, Wis., won by First of America. [Corrected 17:47 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>First of America (corrects from &quot;Dain Bosworth&quot;) said it won $4.195 million of Sheboygan, Wis., general obligation promissory notes, Series 1997 A, with a net interest cost of 4.7454 percent (corrects from &quot;4.7704 percent&quot;).</p>
<p>AMT: 4,195,000	DATE: 02/03/97	NYC Time: 1100     CUSIP: 821022</p>
<p>ISSUER: Sheboygan							ST: WI</p>
<p>ISSUE: General obligation promissory notes, Series 1997A   TAX STAT: Exempt-ULT</p>
<p>M/SP/F: AA3/AA-/NR						     BOOK ENTRY: Y</p>
<p>ENHANCEMENTS: None						     BANK QUAL: Y</p>
<p>DTD: 02/15/97							    SURE BID: Y</p>
<p>DUE: 9/1/98-06						SR MGR: First of America</p>
<p>1ST CPN: 09/01/97					   DOLLAR BID: 100.00</p>
<p>CALL: 9/1/04 @ par					  NIC 4.7454</p>
<p>DELIVERY: 2/18/97 approx				  ORDERS: 1.5 HRS</p>
<p>PAYING AGENT: Finance Director/Treasurer's Office, Sheboygan</p>
<p>L.O.: Foley &amp; Lardner, Milwaukee</p>
<p>F.A.: Griffin, Kubik, Stephens &amp; Thompson, Inc., Milwaukee</p>
<p>LAST SALE: $5,000,000 1/8/96 @ 4.3182% NIC; 6yrs 11mos Avg; BBI-5.37%</p>
